<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russian Provisional Government</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russian Provisional Government governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> from the abdication of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a> in March 1917 until the Bolshevik seizure of power in November 1917. Led first by Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgy-lvov">Georgy Lvov</a> and then by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-kerensky">Alexander Kerensky</a>, it granted civil liberties and in September proclaimed Russia a republic, but lost support by continuing the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and delaying land reform. It was overthrown in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russian-provisional-government.jpg" alt="Russian Provisional Government" width="320" height="301" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Билибин, Иван Яковлевич. Компьютерная обработка: Лобачев Владимир · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Russian_coa_1917.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
